      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "[Github](https://github.com/stuttlepress) | [CivitAI](https://civitai.com/user/__Bob__) \n\n*You're free to do whatever you want with this workflow, but it makes me feel good when you give me credit. Redistributing it without attribution is kind of lame.*\n\n* * *\n\n# How to Use This Workflow\n\n## 1. Install Requirements\n> ### Wan VACE Prep\n> - [Repository](https://github.com/stuttlepress/ComfyUI-Wan-VACE-Prep)\n> - v1.0.19 or higher required\n> - Search *Wan VACE Prep* in ComfyUI Manager\n> - Provides the **🪐 Video Outpaint** node. \n\n\n## 2. Select models appropriate for your system\n- **Select your VACE models** in the *Load* group. Choose models that match what you usually run in your normal Wan workflow. If you usually run FP8 for video generation, choose FP8 VACE models. If you usually use Q4 GGUF, use Q4 GGUF VACE models.\n- **Select or disable lightx2v loras.** Using the same loras and strength that your input clips were generated with may reduce VACE brightness/color artifacts.\n\n## 3. Load your input video\n\n  -  **3.5 (Optional) Configure the video transition**.  \nSet the *extend_from_idx*, *context_frames*, and *new_frames* parameters on the **Wan VACE Extend** node. The defaults work well for 81 frame 16fps clips, but feel free to experiment. Tooltips and the [README file](https://github.com/stuttlepress/ComfyUI-Wan-VACE-Prep/blob/main/README.md#wan-vace-extend) give a little more information about how the parameters work.\n\n## 4. Run the workflow\nThe joined video will be placed in your ComfyUI *output* directory, named something like `VACE_extend_0001.mp4`\n"
